{
  "name": "AI Meeting Notes → Tasks",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🎯 AI MEETING NOTES → TASKS\n**What it does:** A new meeting transcript (.txt/.md) lands in your Google Drive folder → AI extracts every action item (owner, due date, priority) with structured output → each item becomes a Notion task + is logged in Google Sheets → Slack gets the meeting summary, Telegram confirms.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- Google Drive OAuth2 credential (a folder for transcripts)\n- OpenAI API key (platform.openai.com)\n- Notion integration + a Tasks database with columns: `Name` (title), `Owner` (text), `Due` (date), `Priority` (select), `Source` (text)\n- Slack OAuth2 credential (a channel to post summaries)\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID (@BotFather → /newbot)\n\n**Transcripts:** save from any transcription tool (Fireflies, Otter.ai, Whisper) as .txt or .md into the watched Drive folder.\n\n**Status flow in Sheets:** `EXTRACTED` → `CREATED`",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 3440,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "92af9af2-8a8b-474d-8c40-caaae60741a8",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Drive trigger + transcript extraction\nNew file in the transcripts folder (polled every 5 min) → download the file binary → decode to text (truncated at ~12,000 chars with a note).",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e54b78c5-3d93-4650-9af7-4e7048e5edb0",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — AI action-item extraction\nAI Agent reads the transcript → Structured Output Parser returns `meeting_summary` + `action_items[]` (task, owner, due_date, priority). Items with no named owner fall back to the CONFIG default owner.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "bebcf305-8f38-4a67-a1b3-5565012896ac",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        700,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — Notion tasks + Sheets log\nOne item per action item → create a page in your Notion database (Name / Owner / Due / Priority / Source) → append a row to the `Meeting Tasks` sheet with status `CREATED`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 730,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b699e8ab-5d3a-40c9-9ef3-69f2f7033f3a",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1400,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Slack summary + Telegram notification\nAll items are aggregated into one meeting summary + numbered task list → posted to your Slack channel → Telegram confirms how many tasks were created (top 3 listed).",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1070,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e5ea3ecc-008b-48f1-8edc-91ace8f9cad8",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2130,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "event": "fileCreated",
        "triggerOn": "specificFolder",
        "folderToWatch": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "pollTimes": {
